WEBVTT

00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:16.990
We're currently in pursuit of a speeder
heading north on the main thoroughfare.

00:00:17.990 --> 00:00:21.000
So, we got snow, huh?

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:23.410
Requesting backup in the area.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:27.630
Ain't a day for snow like Christmas.

00:00:27.630 --> 00:00:32.760
Remember, Nabarro, we're only giving
you 24 hours for this Christmas release.

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:35.760
It doesn't give you a lotta time to build snowmen.

00:00:36.590 --> 00:00:39.850
Just go cool off for a bit then come back.

00:00:39.850 --> 00:00:44.100
You still got a whole lot of talking left to do.

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:45.900
...maintain vigorous pursuit.

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:03.290
Mr. Nabarro?

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:05.920
Please, take a seat.

00:01:06.580 --> 00:01:08.920
Who the hell are you?

00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:10.880
I'm Jennifer.

00:01:10.880 --> 00:01:14.670
A present from Mr. Big Andy!

00:01:20.890 --> 00:01:24.310
Andy, my man! You've read my mind!

00:01:30.270 --> 00:01:31.860
So, where are we heading?

00:01:32.360 --> 00:01:34.320
Reed... Hotel.

00:02:02.720 --> 00:02:07.890
I walk unsteadily on paths to nowhere

00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:12.020
wondering what I should do right now.

00:02:13.520 --> 00:02:18.490
I play the song you like on the car stereo

00:02:18.660 --> 00:02:23.030
with the volume up and my feelings crystallized

00:02:23.030 --> 00:02:28.670
driving on streets with no crossroads or signals

00:02:28.870 --> 00:02:34.090
with a speed that will catch up with you.

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:38.550
So faraway - let's run!

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:44.850
And let's not bother with the breaks - full throttle.

00:02:45.140 --> 00:02:49.140
Oh someday - one of these days

00:02:49.350 --> 00:02:54.230
You'll be at my place where nobody can find you.

00:02:54.820 --> 00:03:00.320
Whenever you suffer a breakdown one can't see

00:03:00.570 --> 00:03:05.910
depend on me for your repairs.

00:03:06.160 --> 00:03:10.290
So faraway - let's run!

00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:16.500
We'll reset and start again - even at our limit.

00:03:16.710 --> 00:03:20.800
Oh someday - one of these days

00:03:21.010 --> 00:03:26.850
If I'm with you we'll find our dream.

00:03:32.270 --> 00:03:38.070
Christmas 24 Hours

00:04:02.800 --> 00:04:06.430
Oh, Ms. Dahl. Care for some claret punch?

00:04:06.970 --> 00:04:09.270
No alcohol for me tonight.

00:04:09.270 --> 00:04:11.930
But maybe I'll have a ginger tonic.

00:04:11.930 --> 00:04:13.690
Whoo boy.

00:04:13.690 --> 00:04:17.440
I guess hotel investigators don't even get Christmas off.

00:04:20.190 --> 00:04:23.280
When it comes to criminals, there are no Holy Nights.

00:04:24.610 --> 00:04:27.450
Did someone commit another crime?

00:04:27.450 --> 00:04:30.870
There was a rape-murder just one town over.

00:04:34.330 --> 00:04:38.710
The victim was a woman out hitchhiking and the suspect is a sexual deviant.

00:04:38.710 --> 00:04:42.170
All we know about the guy is
that he might be a traveling sort.

00:04:42.590 --> 00:04:47.430
So that means it's quite possible that animal might be in town?

00:04:47.430 --> 00:04:49.010
Very possible.

00:04:49.010 --> 00:04:51.180
He might even be staying at this hotel.

00:04:52.600 --> 00:04:57.230
There were also two street muggings and a jewelry snatching.

00:04:57.230 --> 00:04:59.230
These criminals just keep coming.

00:05:03.110 --> 00:05:04.200
That hit the spot.

00:05:05.110 --> 00:05:07.200
Merry Christmas.

00:05:07.910 --> 00:05:09.830
Merry Christmas.

00:05:38.100 --> 00:05:39.060
Ah!

00:05:39.060 --> 00:05:40.730
You must mean Mr. Duke Togo.

00:05:41.770 --> 00:05:44.440
He checked in at four this afternoon.

00:05:44.440 --> 00:05:45.740
Can I see that for a sec?

00:05:47.700 --> 00:05:49.870
Room 1801.

00:05:50.740 --> 00:05:52.620
Duke Togo.

00:05:53.120 --> 00:05:55.290
Nationality: Brazilian.

00:05:55.290 --> 00:05:57.330
Occupation: writer.

00:05:57.750 --> 00:05:58.750
Writer?

00:06:03.090 --> 00:06:05.380
What's the matter Ms. Dahl?

00:06:06.670 --> 00:06:11.930
D... Don't tell me... last night's murder-
rapist who's now on the run...

00:06:11.930 --> 00:06:13.930
I didn't say that.

00:06:13.930 --> 00:06:19.440
But... I know damn well that man is no writer.

00:06:48.470 --> 00:06:50.010
Care to dance?

00:06:50.010 --> 00:06:52.600
I mean, may I have this dance?

00:06:59.100 --> 00:07:00.900
Sorry...

00:07:03.020 --> 00:07:06.280
...but I have work to do back in my room.

00:07:10.530 --> 00:07:11.860
Work?

00:07:23.630 --> 00:07:25.090
<i>Charlie?</i>

00:07:31.470 --> 00:07:34.180
<i>No one's committing a crime in my hotel!</i>

00:07:45.730 --> 00:07:46.770
What the?

00:07:49.780 --> 00:07:52.280
My arm... my arm!

00:07:55.780 --> 00:07:57.450
Take care of this.

00:07:57.450 --> 00:08:02.160
I don't plan to press charges against this man, Ms. Hotel Detective.

00:08:22.350 --> 00:08:25.770
<i>Now I know he's not just some ordinary man.</i>

00:08:26.810 --> 00:08:29.650
<i>Those piercing, overattentive eyes.</i>

00:08:29.650 --> 00:08:31.820
<i>His nimble yet aggressive speed.</i>

00:08:31.820 --> 00:08:33.200
<i>And...</i>

00:08:33.200 --> 00:08:37.030
<i>...the way he tagged me as the
hotel detective with just one look.</i>

00:08:43.830 --> 00:08:47.670
That son of a bitch! He didn't hafta go break my arm!

00:08:47.670 --> 00:08:50.340
Let's just hope you won't be able to pick any more pockets.

00:08:50.920 --> 00:08:52.090
Fuck you!

00:08:52.590 --> 00:08:56.840
You owe that man a blowjob. He didn't press charges, you know.

00:08:57.340 --> 00:09:00.100
However, you need to get the hell out of my hotel!

00:09:01.060 --> 00:09:04.100
Charlie, next time I see you here, I'll have your balls.

00:09:04.100 --> 00:09:05.100
Are we clear?

00:09:05.690 --> 00:09:07.020
Oww...

00:09:07.020 --> 00:09:10.610
Fuck. That swollen breast pocket of his looked ripe.

00:09:10.610 --> 00:09:15.110
I thought I'd be getting a sitting
duck instead of a Christmas turkey.

00:09:18.990 --> 00:09:21.410
I'll leave you with this parting gift, Dahl.

00:09:21.870 --> 00:09:27.630
That was a handgun I felt in that guy's breast pocket.

00:09:30.840 --> 00:09:32.170
That cocksucker.

00:09:32.170 --> 00:09:34.800
He just fucking winged Charlie the Falcon.

00:10:44.790 --> 00:10:47.870
You probably already know me by now.

00:10:48.750 --> 00:10:50.290
But I'm the investigator for this hotel.

00:10:53.840 --> 00:10:57.300
There's a few questions I need to ask, may I come in?

00:10:59.300 --> 00:11:04.180
If I need to, I can enter by force.

00:11:04.180 --> 00:11:05.810
Will that be necessary?

00:11:20.530 --> 00:11:25.330
It seems that you're a writer, so do you have a notebook somewhere? Or maybe a laptop?

00:11:28.790 --> 00:11:33.330
From where I'm standing, I don't even see a damn pencil laying around anywhere.

00:11:34.540 --> 00:11:37.420
So why didn't you take me up on that dance?

00:11:37.840 --> 00:11:40.840
Were you hiding a pistol in your chest holster?

00:11:43.840 --> 00:11:47.260
Or maybe you got the smell of blood on you.

00:11:48.350 --> 00:11:51.850
You didn't want me to get a whiff of a dead body?

00:12:07.530 --> 00:12:09.250
Will you be leaving?

00:12:10.080 --> 00:12:12.540
I was about to go to sleep.

00:12:13.920 --> 00:12:15.380
I won't be leaving!

00:12:15.380 --> 00:12:20.760
Not until I know who you are and why you came to Reed Hotel!

00:12:20.760 --> 00:12:25.590
Then that's your job to find out, since you're the detective.

00:12:31.730 --> 00:12:32.980
You're right.

00:12:32.980 --> 00:12:37.560
But let me make it clear I don't believe for a second that you're a writer.

00:12:40.400 --> 00:12:43.280
It's my job to protect this hotel.

00:12:43.280 --> 00:12:49.290
Whoever you may be, I won't let you get away with any suspicious behavior in this hotel.

00:12:54.460 --> 00:12:55.920
Even if it costs me my life.

00:13:03.050 --> 00:13:04.300
<i>Now I know.</i>

00:13:05.760 --> 00:13:08.640
<i>That man didn't commit a rape-murder.</i>

00:13:08.640 --> 00:13:11.310
<i>Nor did he mug anybody or steal any jewels.</i>

00:13:11.310 --> 00:13:13.560
<i>He's not some thug that pulls those things.</i>

00:13:16.810 --> 00:13:20.820
<i>If these eyes didn't betray me, what I saw was a pro.</i>

00:13:20.820 --> 00:13:23.570
<i>And a top-ranked criminal mastermind at that!</i>

00:13:36.170 --> 00:13:42.090
<i>Whoever you may be, I won't let you get away with any suspicious behavior in this hotel.</i>

00:13:43.880 --> 00:13:45.170
<i>Even if it costs me my life.</i>

00:13:50.350 --> 00:13:53.180
You asking if I'm all right?

00:13:53.970 --> 00:13:56.850
Maybe you should ask that when I'm done with Jennifer.

00:13:57.980 --> 00:14:03.190
Anyways, thanks for that fantastic present. I owe you one, Andy.

00:14:03.190 --> 00:14:05.740
And you can breathe easy.

00:14:05.740 --> 00:14:11.200
I ain't gonna turn stoolie to no cop about the dirt we do, our syndicate - any of it.

00:14:11.200 --> 00:14:19.790
I only gotta button up for 2, 3 more weeks tops till they're forced to release me.

00:14:21.170 --> 00:14:26.130
Yeah, it's my fuck-up that got me scooped up in the first place. Sorry, okay?

00:14:28.260 --> 00:14:32.470
Look, I'm kinda busy now. We'll talk later, Andy.

00:14:34.470 --> 00:14:41.480
All right, Jennifer. It's been a while since I had some, and I ain't finished yet!

00:14:42.690 --> 00:14:46.320
Did you think I was gonna run out on you screaming?

00:14:46.320 --> 00:14:50.860
Mr. Big Andy gave me enough money to last you till morning!

00:14:52.410 --> 00:14:53.700
Jennifer...

00:14:53.700 --> 00:14:56.250
...you gonna be my little wench or what?

00:14:56.250 --> 00:14:57.830
Oh, Tommy...

00:14:57.830 --> 00:14:59.040
Oh Tommy!

00:15:12.890 --> 00:15:15.970
Good morning, Bill. It sure snowed last night.

00:15:15.970 --> 00:15:17.810
Good morning to you, Ms. Dahl.

00:15:18.520 --> 00:15:20.810
It's a pretty peaceful Christmas morning.

00:15:20.810 --> 00:15:23.810
Has our guest in Room 1801 made any moves?

00:15:23.810 --> 00:15:26.900
Oh, you mean Mr. Duke Togo.

00:15:27.400 --> 00:15:32.570
Well he hasn't done anything in particular. He hasn't even made an outside call.

00:15:32.570 --> 00:15:33.740
Really?

00:15:33.740 --> 00:15:35.330
That mysterious Japanese-Brazilian?

00:15:36.120 --> 00:15:39.790
You seem awfully suspicious of that guest.

00:15:39.790 --> 00:15:41.830
Why is that, Ms. Dahl?

00:15:41.830 --> 00:15:45.840
I suspect any guest who catches my attention. That's my job.

00:16:27.090 --> 00:16:31.420
That was a rocking Christmas Eve, too bad it ended quick.

00:16:32.010 --> 00:16:36.260
I ain't lying, I feel like an fucking new man!

00:16:38.510 --> 00:16:43.190
I gotta be back by ten, so send my regards to Andy.

00:16:48.900 --> 00:16:50.030
Later babe!

00:16:54.950 --> 00:16:59.830
Well, guess I'll take in this morning air with a little stroll.

00:17:06.790 --> 00:17:10.300
Hey, Dahl! Thank God you're here!

00:17:11.460 --> 00:17:12.800
Is there something up?

00:17:13.380 --> 00:17:15.930
Have you seen this man?

00:17:17.550 --> 00:17:19.810
No... who's that?

00:17:20.260 --> 00:17:22.390
The name's Tommy Nabarro.

00:17:22.390 --> 00:17:26.560
He's an underboss for the syndicate run by Andrew Shapiro, aka "Big Andy."

00:17:26.560 --> 00:17:32.440
About two weeks ago my department arrested him for extortion, gambling

00:17:32.440 --> 00:17:37.660
drug-running, sex trafficking, tax evasion, and a whole bunch of other charges.

00:17:37.660 --> 00:17:42.160
But yesterday we gave him a 24-
hour release after he posted bail.

00:17:43.080 --> 00:17:45.790
However, while working late into the night...

00:17:46.790 --> 00:17:48.080
<i>What was that?</i>

00:17:48.080 --> 00:17:50.000
<i>Are you positive?</i>

00:17:50.590 --> 00:17:52.380
<i>Y-Yes understood!</i>

00:17:53.090 --> 00:17:54.590
<i>What's the hubbub?</i>

00:17:55.220 --> 00:17:57.630
<i>It's a tip from the state police.</i>

00:17:57.630 --> 00:18:01.100
<i>It looks like the syndicate is looking to whack Tommy Nabarro.</i>

00:18:01.510 --> 00:18:02.100
<i>What?</i>

00:18:03.100 --> 00:18:05.100
So they're gonna shut him up for good?

00:18:05.100 --> 00:18:06.180
Yeah.

00:18:06.180 --> 00:18:12.360
Also, they're not looking to silence him just to prevent a flood of indictments.

00:18:12.820 --> 00:18:13.900
What do you mean?

00:18:14.360 --> 00:18:21.120
Evidence of a dark link between the syndicate and a
powerful member of the Senate might also be revealed.

00:18:21.530 --> 00:18:25.870
So they're afraid Nabarro might squeal about that fact?

00:18:25.870 --> 00:18:29.290
I've been hunting him down since yesterday.

00:18:29.290 --> 00:18:37.880
This morning I finally got hold of the taxi driver that drove him and a suspected call girl to this hotel.

00:18:38.510 --> 00:18:40.220
Let's get to the reception desk.

00:18:40.220 --> 00:18:45.390
If we ask the building, then we'll know for sure if Nabarro is staying at our hotel.

00:18:45.850 --> 00:18:46.810
Let's do that.

00:18:48.140 --> 00:18:51.150
They must have sent the hit man by now.

00:18:56.990 --> 00:19:00.360
We might end up with a cold body in his room if we don't act quick.

00:19:10.710 --> 00:19:14.250
Ain't nothing like a White Christmas.

00:19:20.800 --> 00:19:25.260
If you're looking for that guest, he
already checked out some time ago.

00:19:25.680 --> 00:19:27.350
So he's still alive and well?

00:19:28.850 --> 00:19:29.640
<i>That guy...</i>

00:19:33.110 --> 00:19:34.110
Oh... hey!

00:19:42.360 --> 00:19:43.370
Huh?

00:20:07.720 --> 00:20:08.640
Dammit!

00:20:17.150 --> 00:20:18.400
Over there!

00:20:23.700 --> 00:20:25.820
That's him! That's Nabarro!

00:20:25.820 --> 00:20:28.120
He was shot in the face.

00:20:31.830 --> 00:20:33.500
Dammit!

00:20:33.500 --> 00:20:36.250
That hit man can't have gone far!

00:21:07.200 --> 00:21:08.030
Hmm?

00:21:08.030 --> 00:21:10.870
Good morning to you, Mr. Togo.

00:21:11.500 --> 00:21:13.290
I need to check out.

00:21:14.290 --> 00:21:15.710
Of course, sir.

00:21:17.750 --> 00:21:20.380
Were you able to relax?

00:21:20.380 --> 00:21:21.630
Yes.

00:21:21.630 --> 00:21:22.590
Thank you.

00:21:26.890 --> 00:21:28.470
Take care.

00:21:36.140 --> 00:21:37.650
About your job...

00:21:38.230 --> 00:21:41.650
I'm not sure how you got him to turn around.

00:21:44.650 --> 00:21:47.610
But, I guess I need to thank you.

00:21:49.030 --> 00:21:51.660
For keeping it out of our hotel.

00:22:40.830 --> 00:22:45.960
I enjoyed the little things.

00:22:48.010 --> 00:22:53.180
I loved when you gave me a flower every day

00:22:53.930 --> 00:22:59.270
instead of just one big bouquet

00:22:59.980 --> 00:23:04.110
of flowers.

00:23:06.190 --> 00:23:11.740
It was like a romance novel.

00:23:12.370 --> 00:23:16.330
Surely someday... just kidding.

00:23:16.660 --> 00:23:19.710
I had a dream.

00:23:20.080 --> 00:23:25.420
Your face shined eternally.

00:23:26.250 --> 00:23:32.010
Because I think of you all the time.

00:23:32.430 --> 00:23:37.560
I'm sorry, but on a lonely night like this

00:23:38.520 --> 00:23:44.060
I'm remembering you, but

00:23:44.360 --> 00:23:48.650
I won't cry like I did that day.

00:23:50.400 --> 00:23:51.820
I won't.

00:24:02.120 --> 00:24:07.840
Sara, a runaway girl, found a peculiar coded message in a stolen wallet

00:24:07.840 --> 00:24:11.260
passed along to her by a fellow pickpocket at the Paris Métro.

00:24:11.930 --> 00:24:15.470
Sara was then chased by a mysterious man seeking to end her life.

00:24:16.260 --> 00:24:21.140
It was Golgo who saved the girl who was running through Paris.

00:24:21.100 --> 00:24:26.900
A Girl Named Sara

00:24:21.730 --> 00:24:25.190
Next time on Golgo 13: A Girl Named Sara.

00:24:25.190 --> 00:24:28.980
Don't stand behind him, if you value your life.
